        "id": "thm-discrete-integers-have-circle-dual",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "The Pontryagin dual of the discrete integers is the circle",
        "statement": "For discrete additive Z, the map Ψ(z)(n)=z^n from the multiplicative unit circle to the Pontryagin dual is a group isomorphism and a homeomorphism; in angular coordinates the characters are n↦e^{inλ}.",
