      {
        "id": "def-time-series-spectral-measure-and-periodogram",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Spectral measures and the known-mean periodogram",
        "statement": "Fix angular frequency on T=R/(2πZ), with unnormalized angular Lebesgue measure dλ. Define a spectral measure F for a weakly stationary real process by γ(h)=∫T e^{ihλ}F(dλ), and define a density only when F is absolutely continuous. Define the known-mean periodogram I_n(λ)=(2πn)^{-1}|Σ_{t=1}^n(X_t−μ)e^{-itλ}|², the normalized Fejér kernel, and the periodized compactly supported kernel smoother on the Fourier grid when its finite normalizer is positive.",
