        "id": "thm-herglotz-spectrum-and-spectral-density",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Herglotz spectral measure and the summable-covariance density",
        "statement": "Assume AC and DC. Every real weakly stationary process indexed by Z has a unique finite positive Radon spectral measure F on the circle with γ(h)=∫T e^{ihλ}F(dλ) and F(T)=γ(0). If Σ_{h∈Z}|γ(h)|<∞, then F has the continuous nonnegative density f(λ)=(2π)^{-1}Σ_{h∈Z}γ(h)e^{-ihλ}.",
