      {
        "id": "thm-periodogram-fejer-expectation-and-smoothing-bias",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Expected periodogram and smoothed spectral-density bias",
        "statement": "The known-mean periodogram has finite-sample expectation (2π)^{-1}Σ_{|h|<n}(1−|h|/n)γ(h)e^{-ihλ}; whenever a spectral measure F is supplied this is ∫T Φ_n(λ−θ)F(dθ), and for F=f dλ it is the Fejér convolution of f. If f∈L¹ is continuous at λ₀ and K is a nonnegative normalized compactly supported continuous kernel with K(0)>0, the kernel-smoothed Fourier-grid estimator with b_n→0 and n b_n→∞ is eventually defined and has expectation tending to f(λ₀).",
        "deps": [
